Test aid, not a fix: a build that forgets every bonded device at each start, once the BLE stack
runs. Flash it, let it start, then flash the build under test: the FlySight has forgotten every
host, and the hosts have not forgotten it.

The firmware itself only does this when USB mode ends with `Reset_BLE: 1` in flysight.txt
(`FS_State_Update()` in FlySight/state.c).

--- a/STM32_WPAN/App/app_ble.c
+++ b/STM32_WPAN/App/app_ble.c
@@ -426,6 +426,9 @@
   Custom_APP_Init();
 
   /* USER CODE BEGIN APP_BLE_Init_3 */
+  /* Test aid: forget every bonded device at each start */
+  aci_gap_clear_security_db();
+
   /* Create timer to handle the connection state machine */
   HW_TS_Create(CFG_TIM_PROC_ID_ISR, &Advertising_mgr_timer_Id, hw_ts_SingleShot, Adv_Update_Req);
 #if 0
